  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Harbor Wall Light",
    "description": "A slim harbor light at the end of a stone harbor wall, its lamp marking the way in for boats coming home. A fishing boat is tied up on the sheltered side. 32 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Harbor Wall** — six grey Block 2x2s in a row run out to sea, and three more across the end make a T-shaped pier head.\n2. **Parapet** — six Low Wall 2x1s along the seaward edge of the wall, to keep the spray off the quay.\n3. **Light Tower** — a Round Plate 2x2 on the pier head, then six Round Bricks stacked red, white, red, white, red, white. A Door faces the harbor.\n4. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2 for the gallery, a yellow Round Brick for the lamp, another Round Plate 2x2 above it and a red Cone Roof on top.\n5. **Moorings** — two dark Half Cubes for bollards on the sheltered side of the wall, and a fishing boat between them: a Plate 2x4 hull turned 90° (press **R**), a blue Half Cube for the wheelhouse and a Post for the mast.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Harbor Wall: 9 Block 2x2\n- Parapet: 6 Low Wall 2x1\n- Light Tower: 1 Round Plate 2x2, 6 Round Brick, 1 Door\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Round Brick, 1 Cone Roof\n- Moorings: 3 Half Cube, 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Post\n\n32 bricks in all.\n",
